# AOSB VMS Coding Standards

## Python

- Write clean, self-explaining Python with **explicit type hints** on functions and methods.
- Add **concise inline comments** only for critical business or compliance logic (e.g. document expiry rules, status locks, ISO workflow gates).
- For complex blocks, briefly explain *why* the logic exists so another developer can debug it.

## Django forms & documents

- Use **Django Form / ModelForm** validation for document uploads and expiry dates — do not rely on ad-hoc view checks alone.
- Reject invalid PDFs, missing dates, and expired/invalid date ranges in `clean()` / field validators.

## Templates & Tailwind

- Style **only** with Tailwind CSS utility classes inside HTML templates (no bespoke CSS frameworks).
- Keep templates under `/templates` with reusable components (`sidebar`, `header`, `status_badge`, etc.).
- Prefer `{% include %}` for shared chrome; keep page templates thin.

## Secrets & environment

- **Never** hardcode or commit secret keys, tokens, or database passwords.
- Load all secrets via **django-environ** from `.env` (see `.env.example`).
- Keep `.env` out of git; document new variables in `.env.example` without real values.
